To explain this system, the hypen represents a null sound, nybble #0
uses some consonant pairs that take on the voicing of the consonant
used in nybble #1,  and nybble #2 is really an emphasis bit followed
by a 3-bit number representing some non-consonants. I haven't really
come up with a good way to write this yet. Using a vertical bar to
break up syllables, here are some Lojban words in this system:

bangrsperanto
-b-A|ng-r|sp-e|-,rA|nt-o

sumti tcita
-s-U|mt-i|tc-I|-t-a

la bastyn.
--la|-b-A|st-y|n.--

Something I just thought, nybble #2 will probably never use {my} or {ny}.


